\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Hydrodynamic collapse in Conformal MIS ($N = 20\,000$ points, $K_{\mathrm  {opt}} = 100$).} (a) Scatter slices across proper time $\tau $ showing the thinning trajectory cloud. (b) Stacked histograms of local dimension $d_{\mathrm  {PR}}$ under optimal $K_{\mathrm  {opt}} = 100$, color-segmented into 8 layers of initial anisotropy $\mathcal  {A}_0$. The three stages of hydrodynamization are manifested: pure 2D unimodality at $\tau \le 0.35\,\mathrm  {fm}/c$, clean bimodality separating the attractor core and relaxing wings at $\tau = 0.55\,\mathrm  {fm}/c$, and asymptotic 1D collapse at $\tau \ge 0.80\,\mathrm  {fm}/c$.}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
